Vendored test fixtures from the Claude Code plugin directory.

Source:  https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official
Commit:  d182ca456ca09d31d139f7d3818d1d333b103cce
License: each plugin directory carries its own LICENSE file (Apache License
         2.0), vendored beside it unchanged.

Directories and their paths in the source repository:

  hookify/            <- plugins/hookify/
  security-guidance/  <- plugins/security-guidance/
  feature-dev/        <- plugins/feature-dev/

Every file other than a script is a byte-for-byte copy of the source at that
commit. The scripts (every *.py and *.sh file) are zero-byte placeholders of
the same name: the reader never opens a hook's script, and these tests read
what a plugin declares, never run it. Nothing under this directory is
formatted, linted or edited; a change here is a re-vendoring at a new commit
and updates this notice.
